}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"534fe629e37ac3976c185d424e4a25c402f673bcfb43dc427356103277029f6b","event_uuid":"b8d5fca9-c8fb-424f-b5c1-5de8a510538c","position":{"commit_sha":"af636b34efbd690c646c77278e7c4393c4bb9c51","position":"1785725599707836001-b8d5fca9-c8fb-424f-b5c1-5de8a510538c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"28fd48448f7b1cd335cb90315105073509cae252ddd4bb9a1af6084cd18423b0","event_uuid":"329a3d92-8960-4660-b5cc-d268f6a6c515","position":{"commit_sha":"bc87f7090d0b69b9582f41b0454043a562c539de","position":"1785725981413065001-329a3d92-8960-4660-b5cc-d268f6a6c515"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root cause: material_fingerprint (pass1.py) hashed the raw description, so the box-flip that 433c's close precheck REQUIRES read as a material edit -> stale-material -> forced re-review before every close (observed on d3ed/433c/9d07/a584 closes).\n\nFix pushed as Gerrit change 1262: _normalize_checkbox_state erases box STATE (line-anchored, -/* bullets, x/X) before hashing; item text stays material. Both staleness consumers (plan-review close gate + completion-verifier stale-material) recompute through this one seam via current_material_fingerprint, so one normalization covers both. Pinned-literal fingerprint tests unchanged (review-time descriptions are unchecked -> byte-identical basis). 3 RED tests first (unit invariance x2, store-level attestation validity), mutation-checked (line-dropping over-normalization killed by item-text-edit + indent tests). 206 neighborhood tests green.\n\nUntil 1262 merges, closes on stores driven by pre-fix builds still trip stale-material; workaround remains re-running review-plan before close.","timestamp":1785725981413065001}],"created_at":1785725580237332001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6e3d1a96-16c8-4e09-aca2-7f2b2959fe98","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"433c-aa00-8ac1-49ae"}],"description":"## Context\n433c requires AC boxes checked before close; but checking a box edits the description, and material_fingerprint (llm/plan_review/pass1.py) hashes the raw description — so the required box-flip trips stale-material in validate_attestation (attest.py) and forces a fresh LLM review before EVERY close. Observed on all four closes of d3ed/433c/9d07/a584. Checkbox STATE is progress metadata (verified independently by the completion verifier); the ITEM TEXT is the material.\n\n## Approach\nNormalize checkbox state before hashing in material_fingerprint: case-insensitive `- [x]`/`- [X]` → `- [ ]` (also `*` bullets), line-anchored, so flipping a box never changes the fingerprint while ANY text change still does. Single seam: both the plan-review close gate and the completion-verifier staleness check recompute through material_fingerprint via current_material_fingerprint.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py (material_fingerprint: normalize description basis)\n- tests: unit on fingerprint invariance + a close-gate-level regression\n\n## Testing\nRED first: fingerprint(desc with [ ]) == fingerprint(desc with [x]) fails today; any non-checkbox text edit still changes the fingerprint; validate_attestation no longer returns stale-material after a pure box flip.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Flipping any AC box (either direction, x or X, - or * bullet) leaves the material fingerprint unchanged.\n- [ ] Any other description edit still changes the fingerprint (staleness preserved).\n- [ ] A signed plan-review attestation stays valid across a pure box-flip edit (no stale-material at close).\n- [ ] Existing attestations signed on unchecked descriptions remain valid for checked descriptions (normalization is backward-compatible by construction).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6252e018-bfd8-43ec-9024-3c5e909ecb6f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"330c-1c85-5bd4-48b5","ticket_type":"bug","title":"AC checkbox flips invalidate plan-review attestation (stale-material on every close)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e33ed06c-a0aa-42f6-b027-d464ee28eeea","6e3d1a96-16c8-4e09-aca2-7f2b2959fe98","6252e018-bfd8-43ec-9024-3c5e909ecb6f","b8d5fca9-c8fb-424f-b5c1-5de8a510538c","329a3d92-8960-4660-b5cc-d268f6a6c515"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785725981413065002,"uuid":"e8640bb9-47f6-4740-9bea-e40bd4a09f75"}